{"title":"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A black pawn and a white pawn are placed on the first square and the last square of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27c43e5796d05a1f8593a5c9307fc0fc5ef1e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> chessboard, respectively. Wiwit and Siti move alternatingly. Wiwit has the white pawn, and Siti has the black pawn. The white pawn moves first. In every move, the player moves her pawn one or two squares to the right or to the left, without passing the opponent's pawn. The first player who cannot move anymore loses the game. Which player has the winning strategy? Explain the strategy.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can try out the game with smaller values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then black wins (since white can't move).  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then white wins (since white can move forward one space to corner black).  Similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, then white wins (since white can move forward two spaces to corner black).\n</p><p><br />\nAdditionally, note that if the first player decides to move backwards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> spaces, then the second player can move forwards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> spaces to maintain the number of spaces between the first player and the second player.  Same goes for if the second player moves backwards.  Thus, if the two pieces are adjacent to each other and it is the first player's turn, then the first player would lose because the second player can force the first player back to the end of the playing area (same for the second player).\n</p><p><br />\nWith this in mind, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then black would win because moving one space forward would put white in black's position in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and moving two spaces would put white in black's position in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.  Additionally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then white would win because by moving one, white would force black in white's position in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec37f4048b4f92c2227c9bfe79fcb7d52ab99c9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea0402efce9f2319988b2f404519983e0e8ff93e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 7$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, then white would win by moving two.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we can suspect that black would win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5cbead4d646c454c8dea87c89076d7f30e961f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and white would in otherwise, and we can prove by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a>.  We already have the base case covered in the above paragraphs.  For the inductive step, assume that black would win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65857424dc23a16818f661ecb638b81cebad9710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> and white would win in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5602da83a2fe621a9dec8028934013def3c9c481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e4c544ed874eae477f377d075a0dcf58561e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />.  Since white moves first, we can note that the second player moving would win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65857424dc23a16818f661ecb638b81cebad9710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> and the first player would win otherwise.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f95bd6e1ccc8d0f1235954024aefa5b3fad7d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, white moving forward one space means that black can move two spaces forward to put white at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65857424dc23a16818f661ecb638b81cebad9710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, and white moving forward two spaces means that black can move one space forward to put white at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65857424dc23a16818f661ecb638b81cebad9710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, so black (or the second player) would win.  However, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/01312031c24df323102fbe42c8967429ff45441a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, white can move forward 1 to force black in white's position in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f95bd6e1ccc8d0f1235954024aefa5b3fad7d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66bb20cce143c1a2aa237cd53bd7c749b116f746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, white can move forward 2 to force black in white's position in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f95bd6e1ccc8d0f1235954024aefa5b3fad7d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, so white would win in both scenarios.\n</p><p><br />\nSince white and black can copy the opponent moving backward, moving backwards would not affect the results.  Thus, by induction, black would win if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5cbead4d646c454c8dea87c89076d7f30e961f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> by moving forward 1 if white moves forward 2 and moving forward 2 if white moves forward 1, and white would win otherwise by moving forward 1 if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1e98d144514989484036a3122ce2aec6c1ac257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> or by moving forward 2 if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0cb3b40200856bf02df3c0604e1598550ce0ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and then moving forward 1 if black moves forward 2 and moving forward 2 if black moves forward 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO\">2006 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211747\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 179/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1044/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4785/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.659      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    6.659  